          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can be sure of the existence of a triangle only if we can show that the circles intersect internally (as in Fig. 7.5) whenever the triangle inequality is satisfied. But are there other possibilities when the two circles are constructed? Let us visualise and study them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.162,
            0.648,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The following different cases can be conceived:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
