            0.175,
            0.543,
            0.657,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that while constructing the circles, we take"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.569,
            0.714,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) the length of the base AB = longest of the given length"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.591,
            0.698,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) the radii of the circles to be the smaller two lengths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.615,
            0.848,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Which of the above-mentioned cases will lead to the formation of a triangle? Clearly, triangles are formed only when the circles intersect each other internally (Case 3)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.678,
